window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b265-c4eef95c8343a0af.json"]={sha256:"c4eef95c8343a0af6dc2086b0037ce8777f5c88a242fb85b03b0e31653423371",value:{"id":"b265","title":"配水管網壓力管理","titleEn":"Pressure management of water-distribution networks","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課從高程與服務壓力出發，分析壓力相依需求、漏失指數及閥門耗能，再進入閥權度、遠端延遲、回授方向和備援供水。最後把快速水錘與低流量水質納入同一管理問題，讓節水效益與服務可靠度各有證據，不把降低平均壓力當成唯一成功指標。","summaryEn":"Beginning with elevation and service pressure, this course examines pressure-dependent demand, leakage exponents and valve dissipation, then addresses authority, remote delay, feedback direction and backup supply. Rapid transients and low-flow water quality complete the management problem, giving savings and service reliability separate evidence instead of treating lower average pressure as the only success metric.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-pipe","architectureNodes":[["服務與地形","Service and terrain"],["管網與漏口","Network and leaks"],["減壓閥與回授","Reducing valve and feedback"],["備援及瞬變","Backup and transients"],["成效與水質","Performance and quality"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-pipe","labels":["服務與地形","管網與漏口","減壓閥與回授","備援及瞬變","成效與水質"],"labelsEn":["Service and terrain","Network and leaks","Reducing valve and feedback","Backup and transients","Performance and quality"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創敏感度例設定同一漏口群的初始漏失10 L/s、代表壓力水頭40 m，降至30 m後若採固定孔口指數N=0.5，漏失為8.660 L/s；若改用假設校準指數N=1.2，則為7.081 L/s。兩個模型分別預測13.4%與29.2%的減少，差異來自模型而非新的現場量測。應用獨立資料校準指數，同時檢查高處服務壓力、閥動作水錘及低更新支線水質。不得選擇看起來節水較多的指數來替代驗證，也不能將本例壓力寫成真實控制設定。","textEn":"An original sensitivity example uses the same leak population with initial leakage 10 L/s at representative head 40 m. Reducing head to 30 m gives 8.660 L/s with fixed-orifice exponent N=0.5, or 7.081 L/s with hypothetical calibrated exponent N=1.2. The predicted reductions are 13.4% and 29.2%; the difference comes from the model rather than new field observations. Calibrate the exponent independently while checking elevated-customer pressure, valve-induced transients and quality in low-renewal branches. Choosing the exponent that promises greater savings cannot replace validation, and the assumed heads are not real control settings.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b265-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證」與「壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification\" and \"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b265-v15-01","title":"高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「高程水頭與服務壓力」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elevation head and service pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓力管理要控制的是用戶與關鍵設施可取得的壓力，不能只追求減壓閥出口的一個數字。節點水頭包含高程與壓力，沿途摩阻又隨需求變動，因此低處壓力過高時，高處仍可能接近供水不足；管理分區需同時考慮高程帶、管路阻力與代表性服務點。下式分開能量水頭、高程及流動損失，忽略速度水頭差；所得壓力水頭只適用指定需求工況，不代表全天最小值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高程水頭與服務壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pressure management concerns pressure available to customers and critical facilities, not merely one number at a reducing-valve outlet. Nodal head includes elevation and pressure, while friction changes with demand. A low-lying area can have excessive pressure while an elevated area approaches insufficient supply, so zoning must consider elevation bands, resistance and representative service points together. The relation separates energy head, elevation and losses while neglecting velocity-head differences. The resulting pressure head applies to one demand condition, not the daily minimum. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elevation head and service pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設供水水頭H=100 m、節點高程z=60 m、路徑損失hf=15 m，壓力水頭h=H−z−hf=25 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume supply head H=100 m, node elevation z=60 m and path loss hf=15 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高程水頭與服務壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elevation head and service pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-01-k1","title":"高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證","titleEn":"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification","text":"壓力管理要控制的是用戶與關鍵設施可取得的壓力，不能只追求減壓閥出口的一個數字。節點水頭包含高程與壓力，沿途摩阻又隨需求變動，因此低處壓力過高時，高處仍可能接近供水不足；管理分區需同時考慮高程帶、管路阻力與代表性服務點。","textEn":"Pressure management concerns pressure available to customers and critical facilities, not merely one number at a reducing-valve outlet. Nodal head includes elevation and pressure, while friction changes with demand.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。","壓力管理要控制的是用戶與關鍵設施可取得的壓力，不能只追求減壓閥出口的一個數字。","管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer.","Pressure management concerns pressure available to customers and critical facilities, not merely one number at a reducing-valve outlet.","A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"壓力管理要控制的是用戶與關鍵設施可取得的壓力，不能只追求減壓閥出口的一個數字。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pressure management concerns pressure available to customers and critical facilities, not merely one number at a reducing-valve outlet. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b265-v15-02","title":"高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高程水頭與服務壓力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elevation head and service pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設供水水頭H=100 m、節點高程z=60 m、路徑損失hf=15 m，壓力水頭h=H−z−hf=25 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume supply head H=100 m, node elevation z=60 m and path loss hf=15 m. Pressure head h=H−z−hf=25 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將關鍵服務點的高程、壓力與需求時間對齊，核對感測器讀值是表壓或水頭。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align elevations, pressure and demand times at critical service points, checking whether sensors report gauge pressure or head.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設供水水頭H=100 m、節點高程z=60 m、路徑損失hf=15 m，壓力水頭h=H−z−hf=25 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume supply head H=100 m, node elevation z=60 m and path loss hf=15 m. Pressure head h=H−z−hf=25 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。","通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設供水水頭H=100 m、節點高程z=60 m、路徑損失hf=15 m，壓力水頭h=H−z−hf=25 m。"],"optionsEn":["All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity.","A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume supply head H=100 m, node elevation z=60 m and path loss hf=15 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設供水水頭H=100 m、節點高程z=60 m、路徑損失hf=15 m，壓力水頭h=H−z−hf=25 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume supply head H=100 m, node elevation z=60 m and path loss hf=15 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b265-v15-03","title":"高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高程水頭與服務壓力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elevation head and service pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將關鍵服務點的高程、壓力與需求時間對齊，核對感測器讀值是表壓或水頭。比較尖峰與低需求兩個時段的水頭線，檢查閥後量測是否能代表最不利用戶而非只代表附近低點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align elevations, pressure and demand times at critical service points, checking whether sensors report gauge pressure or head. Compare hydraulic grades at peak and low demand and test whether the downstream sensor represents the limiting customer rather than a nearby low point. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：繪出高低兩個服務點在相同閥後水頭下的壓力差，加入需求增加造成的摩阻。列出應監測的最不利位置，避免只以平均區壓決定管理策略。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw pressures at high and low service points under one valve-outlet head and add demand-dependent friction. Identify limiting monitoring locations instead of selecting management strategy from average district pressure alone.","failure":"注意干擾：只在減壓閥附近量到足夠壓力，可能漏掉遠端或高處缺壓；若把地面高程錯當管線量測基準，模型又會把壓力不足誤判成儀器偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adequate pressure near a reducing valve can conceal shortages at remote or elevated users. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將關鍵服務點的高程、壓力與需求時間對齊，核對感測器讀值是表壓或水頭。比較尖峰與低需求兩個時段的水頭線，檢查閥後量測是否能代表最不利用戶而非只代表附近低點。","textEn":"Align elevations, pressure and demand times at critical service points, checking whether sensors report gauge pressure or head. Compare hydraulic grades at peak and low demand and test whether the downstream sensor represents the limiting customer rather than a nearby low point.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"繪出高低兩個服務點在相同閥後水頭下的壓力差，加入需求增加造成的摩阻。列出應監測的最不利位置，避免只以平均區壓決定管理策略。","textEn":"Draw pressures at high and low service points under one valve-outlet head and add demand-dependent friction. Identify limiting monitoring locations instead of selecting management strategy from average district pressure alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將關鍵服務點的高程、壓力與需求時間對齊，核對感測器讀值是表壓或水頭。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。"],"optionsEn":["Align elevations, pressure and demand times at critical service points, checking whether sensors report gauge pressure or head.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將關鍵服務點的高程、壓力與需求時間對齊，核對感測器讀值是表壓或水頭。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align elevations, pressure and demand times at critical service points, checking whether sensors report gauge pressure or head. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b265-v15-04","title":"高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高程水頭與服務壓力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elevation head and service pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只在減壓閥附近量到足夠壓力，可能漏掉遠端或高處缺壓；若把地面高程錯當管線量測基準，模型又會把壓力不足誤判成儀器偏差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adequate pressure near a reducing valve can conceal shortages at remote or elevated users. Confusing ground elevation with the pressure-measurement datum can then misclassify a genuine pressure deficit as instrument error. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：下式分開能量水頭、高程及流動損失，忽略速度水頭差；所得壓力水頭只適用指定需求工況，不代表全天最小值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The resulting pressure head applies to one demand condition, not the daily minimum.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只在減壓閥附近量到足夠壓力，可能漏掉遠端或高處缺壓；若把地面高程錯當管線量測基準，模型又會把壓力不足誤判成儀器偏差。","textEn":"Adequate pressure near a reducing valve can conceal shortages at remote or elevated users. Confusing ground elevation with the pressure-measurement datum can then misclassify a genuine pressure deficit as instrument error.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只在減壓閥附近量到足夠壓力，可能漏掉遠端或高處缺壓；若把地面高程錯當管線量測基準，模型又會把壓力不足誤判成儀器偏差。","管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Adequate pressure near a reducing valve can conceal shortages at remote or elevated users.","A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只在減壓閥附近量到足夠壓力，可能漏掉遠端或高處缺壓；若把地面高程錯當管線量測基準，模型又會把壓力不足誤判成儀器偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adequate pressure near a reducing valve can conceal shortages at remote or elevated users. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b265-v15-05","title":"壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「壓力相依需求與缺水量」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"傳統固定需求模型可能在壓力不足時仍要求節點供出全部流量，造成不合理的負壓結果。壓力相依需求把可供流量連到可用壓力區間，使缺水成為可量化輸出；但需求曲線仍是模型假設，不能將所有用戶、儲水設備與消防用途視為相同的孔口行為。此例採分段模型：低於最低水頭供量為零，達要求水頭供滿量，中間以平方根插值；參數不是任何地方服務標準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓力相依需求與缺水量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A fixed-demand model can require full delivery even when pressure is insufficient, producing unrealistic negative pressures. Pressure-dependent demand relates available flow to a pressure range and makes supply deficit an explicit output. The demand curve remains an assumption, however, and customers, storage installations and fire-service functions cannot all be treated as identical orifices. The example sets zero delivery below minimum head, full delivery at required head and square-root interpolation between them. Its parameters are not jurisdictional service standards. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設需求qreq=20 L/s、hmin=10 m、hreq=30 m、實際h=20 m，q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume required demand qreq=20 L/s, hmin=10 m, hreq=30 m and actual h=20 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓力相依需求與缺水量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-05-k1","title":"壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification","text":"傳統固定需求模型可能在壓力不足時仍要求節點供出全部流量，造成不合理的負壓結果。壓力相依需求把可供流量連到可用壓力區間，使缺水成為可量化輸出；但需求曲線仍是模型假設，不能將所有用戶、儲水設備與消防用途視為相同的孔口行為。","textEn":"A fixed-demand model can require full delivery even when pressure is insufficient, producing unrealistic negative pressures. Pressure-dependent demand relates available flow to a pressure range and makes supply deficit an explicit output.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。","漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。","傳統固定需求模型可能在壓力不足時仍要求節點供出全部流量，造成不合理的負壓結果。"],"optionsEn":["A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow.","The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.","A fixed-demand model can require full delivery even when pressure is insufficient, producing unrealistic negative pressures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"傳統固定需求模型可能在壓力不足時仍要求節點供出全部流量，造成不合理的負壓結果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A fixed-demand model can require full delivery even when pressure is insufficient, producing unrealistic negative pressures. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b265-v15-06","title":"壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓力相依需求與缺水量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設需求qreq=20 L/s、hmin=10 m、hreq=30 m、實際h=20 m，q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume required demand qreq=20 L/s, hmin=10 m, hreq=30 m and actual h=20 m. Delivered q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較固定需求與壓力相依模型在相同邊界下的供量與低壓分布，查核用戶類別與儲水設備是否需不同描述。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare fixed and pressure-dependent demand models under identical boundaries, examining delivery and low-pressure distribution.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設需求qreq=20 L/s、hmin=10 m、hreq=30 m、實際h=20 m，q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume required demand qreq=20 L/s, hmin=10 m, hreq=30 m and actual h=20 m. Delivered q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設需求qreq=20 L/s、hmin=10 m、hreq=30 m、實際h=20 m，q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s。","控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。","比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume required demand qreq=20 L/s, hmin=10 m, hreq=30 m and actual h=20 m.","A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow.","Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設需求qreq=20 L/s、hmin=10 m、hreq=30 m、實際h=20 m，q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume required demand qreq=20 L/s, hmin=10 m, hreq=30 m and actual h=20 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b265-v15-07","title":"壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓力相依需求與缺水量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較固定需求與壓力相依模型在相同邊界下的供量與低壓分布，查核用戶類別與儲水設備是否需不同描述。用可取得的壓力及服務資料驗證缺水量，不只要求數值迭代收斂。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare fixed and pressure-dependent demand models under identical boundaries, examining delivery and low-pressure distribution. Check whether customer categories and storage installations need different representations, and validate deficits using available pressure and service data rather than accepting numerical convergence alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以三個水頭值跨越最低與要求界線，檢查分段需求是否連續且不超過滿額需求。再說明哪些用戶資料可支持參數，而哪些仍應保留敏感度範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: Evaluate three heads spanning minimum and required limits, checking continuity and the full-demand cap. Explain which customer observations support the parameters and which uncertainties should remain as sensitivity ranges.","failure":"注意干擾：以固定需求強迫缺壓節點繼續滿額供水會低估服務中斷，反之把假設需求曲線當精確行為也會製造過度確定的缺水預測；兩者都可能錯排優先改善區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Forcing full demand at a pressure-deficient node understates service disruption, while treating an assumed demand curve as exact behavior creates false certainty in deficit estimates. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較固定需求與壓力相依模型在相同邊界下的供量與低壓分布，查核用戶類別與儲水設備是否需不同描述。用可取得的壓力及服務資料驗證缺水量，不只要求數值迭代收斂。","textEn":"Compare fixed and pressure-dependent demand models under identical boundaries, examining delivery and low-pressure distribution. Check whether customer categories and storage installations need different representations, and validate deficits using available pressure and service data rather than accepting numerical convergence alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以三個水頭值跨越最低與要求界線，檢查分段需求是否連續且不超過滿額需求。再說明哪些用戶資料可支持參數，而哪些仍應保留敏感度範圍。","textEn":"Evaluate three heads spanning minimum and required limits, checking continuity and the full-demand cap. Explain which customer observations support the parameters and which uncertainties should remain as sensitivity ranges.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較固定需求與壓力相依模型在相同邊界下的供量與低壓分布，查核用戶類別與儲水設備是否需不同描述。","平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare fixed and pressure-dependent demand models under identical boundaries, examining delivery and low-pressure distribution.","Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較固定需求與壓力相依模型在相同邊界下的供量與低壓分布，查核用戶類別與儲水設備是否需不同描述。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare fixed and pressure-dependent demand models under identical boundaries, examining delivery and low-pressure distribution. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b265-v15-08","title":"壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓力相依需求與缺水量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以固定需求強迫缺壓節點繼續滿額供水會低估服務中斷，反之把假設需求曲線當精確行為也會製造過度確定的缺水預測；兩者都可能錯排優先改善區。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Forcing full demand at a pressure-deficient node understates service disruption, while treating an assumed demand curve as exact behavior creates false certainty in deficit estimates. Both can misdirect improvement priorities. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此例採分段模型：低於最低水頭供量為零，達要求水頭供滿量，中間以平方根插值；參數不是任何地方服務標準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Its parameters are not jurisdictional service standards.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以固定需求強迫缺壓節點繼續滿額供水會低估服務中斷，反之把假設需求曲線當精確行為也會製造過度確定的缺水預測；兩者都可能錯排優先改善區。","textEn":"Forcing full demand at a pressure-deficient node understates service disruption, while treating an assumed demand curve as exact behavior creates false certainty in deficit estimates. Both can misdirect improvement priorities.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。","以固定需求強迫缺壓節點繼續滿額供水會低估服務中斷，反之把假設需求曲線當精確行為也會製造過度確定的缺水預測；兩者都可能錯排優先改善區。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.","Forcing full demand at a pressure-deficient node understates service disruption, while treating an assumed demand curve as exact behavior creates false certainty in deficit estimates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以固定需求強迫缺壓節點繼續滿額供水會低估服務中斷，反之把假設需求曲線當精確行為也會製造過度確定的缺水預測；兩者都可能錯排優先改善區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Forcing full demand at a pressure-deficient node understates service disruption, while treating an assumed demand curve as exact behavior creates false certainty in deficit estimates. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b265-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證」與「減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification\" and \"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b265-v15-09","title":"漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「漏口變形與壓力指數」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Leak deformation and pressure exponent” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"降低壓力通常能降低既有漏口流量，但效果取決於漏口是否隨壓力張開、材料拘束及不同漏點的組合。固定孔口平方根關係不一定代表整區漏失，經驗指數也不是材料常數；若合法用水、閥位或漏點數同時改變，觀測到的曲線便不能單獨歸因於壓力。本式比較相同漏口群、代表壓力定義不變的兩個狀態，不預測新破口發生率；指數須在適用範圍內校準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漏口變形與壓力指數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reducing pressure generally reduces flow through existing leaks, but the effect depends on opening deformation, restraint and the mix of leaks. A fixed-orifice square-root relation need not represent district leakage, and an empirical exponent is not a material constant. Simultaneous changes in authorized use, valve state or leak count prevent attributing an observed curve to pressure alone. The relation compares the same leak population under a consistent representative-pressure definition. It does not predict new-break frequency, and its exponent requires calibration within the applicable range. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Leak deformation and pressure exponent” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭由40 m降至30 m、漏失指數N=1.2，Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081；假設原漏失10 L/s，則為7.081 L/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head falls from 40 m to 30 m and leakage exponent N=1.2.","failure":"常見誤解：「漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漏口變形與壓力指數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Leak deformation and pressure exponent”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-09-k1","title":"漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證","titleEn":"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification","text":"降低壓力通常能降低既有漏口流量，但效果取決於漏口是否隨壓力張開、材料拘束及不同漏點的組合。固定孔口平方根關係不一定代表整區漏失，經驗指數也不是材料常數；若合法用水、閥位或漏點數同時改變，觀測到的曲線便不能單獨歸因於壓力。","textEn":"Reducing pressure generally reduces flow through existing leaks, but the effect depends on opening deformation, restraint and the mix of leaks. A fixed-orifice square-root relation need not represent district leakage, and an empirical exponent is not a material constant.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["降低壓力通常能降低既有漏口流量，但效果取決於漏口是否隨壓力張開、材料拘束及不同漏點的組合。","漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。","減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。"],"optionsEn":["Reducing pressure generally reduces flow through existing leaks, but the effect depends on opening deformation, restraint and the mix of leaks.","The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.","All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"降低壓力通常能降低既有漏口流量，但效果取決於漏口是否隨壓力張開、材料拘束及不同漏點的組合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reducing pressure generally reduces flow through existing leaks, but the effect depends on opening deformation, restraint and the mix of leaks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b265-v15-10","title":"漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漏口變形與壓力指數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Leak deformation and pressure exponent” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭由40 m降至30 m、漏失指數N=1.2，Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081；假設原漏失10 L/s，則為7.081 L/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head falls from 40 m to 30 m and leakage exponent N=1.2. Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081; assumed initial leakage 10 L/s becomes 7.081 L/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在需求及邊界可比的觀測時段配對壓力與漏失估計，將修復或新爆管事件另外標記。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair pressure and leakage estimates over comparable demand and boundary conditions, marking repairs and new bursts separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭由40 m降至30 m、漏失指數N=1.2，Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081；假設原漏失10 L/s，則為7.081 L/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head falls from 40 m to 30 m and leakage exponent N=1.2. Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081; assumed initial leakage 10 L/s becomes 7.081 L/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭由40 m降至30 m、漏失指數N=1.2，Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081。","現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。"],"optionsEn":["A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head falls from 40 m to 30 m and leakage exponent N=1.2.","Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭由40 m降至30 m、漏失指數N=1.2，Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081；假設原漏失10 L/s，則為7.081 L/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head falls from 40 m to 30 m and leakage exponent N=1.2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b265-v15-11","title":"漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漏口變形與壓力指數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Leak deformation and pressure exponent” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在需求及邊界可比的觀測時段配對壓力與漏失估計，將修復或新爆管事件另外標記。用多個壓力點檢查代表區壓是否合理，並把指數擬合殘差與預測範圍共同呈現。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair pressure and leakage estimates over comparable demand and boundary conditions, marking repairs and new bursts separately. Use several pressure locations to test the representative district pressure and present exponent-fit residuals together with the prediction range. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用固定孔口指數與另一個假設經驗指數比較同一壓力變化，列出結果差異。把減少既有漏流與降低新破管風險分成兩個需不同證據的問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare one pressure change using a fixed-orifice exponent and another hypothetical fitted exponent. Separate reduction of existing leakage from prevention of new breaks, identifying the different evidence needed for each.","failure":"注意干擾：若把修復後漏點減少的效果算進壓力指數，會高估下一次減壓效益；相反，合法夜用水增加也可能掩蓋真實漏失下降，讓管理措施被誤判無效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Including leak removal from repairs in a pressure exponent overstates the benefit of a later pressure reduction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在需求及邊界可比的觀測時段配對壓力與漏失估計，將修復或新爆管事件另外標記。用多個壓力點檢查代表區壓是否合理，並把指數擬合殘差與預測範圍共同呈現。","textEn":"Pair pressure and leakage estimates over comparable demand and boundary conditions, marking repairs and new bursts separately. Use several pressure locations to test the representative district pressure and present exponent-fit residuals together with the prediction range.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用固定孔口指數與另一個假設經驗指數比較同一壓力變化，列出結果差異。把減少既有漏流與降低新破管風險分成兩個需不同證據的問題。","textEn":"Compare one pressure change using a fixed-orifice exponent and another hypothetical fitted exponent. Separate reduction of existing leakage from prevention of new breaks, identifying the different evidence needed for each.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。","在需求及邊界可比的觀測時段配對壓力與漏失估計，將修復或新爆管事件另外標記。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality.","Pair pressure and leakage estimates over comparable demand and boundary conditions, marking repairs and new bursts separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在需求及邊界可比的觀測時段配對壓力與漏失估計，將修復或新爆管事件另外標記。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair pressure and leakage estimates over comparable demand and boundary conditions, marking repairs and new bursts separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b265-v15-12","title":"漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漏口變形與壓力指數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Leak deformation and pressure exponent” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把修復後漏點減少的效果算進壓力指數，會高估下一次減壓效益；相反，合法夜用水增加也可能掩蓋真實漏失下降，讓管理措施被誤判無效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Including leak removal from repairs in a pressure exponent overstates the benefit of a later pressure reduction. Conversely, increased legitimate night use can hide real leakage reduction and make the measure appear ineffective. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本式比較相同漏口群、代表壓力定義不變的兩個狀態，不預測新破口發生率；指數須在適用範圍內校準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not predict new-break frequency, and its exponent requires calibration within the applicable range.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把修復後漏點減少的效果算進壓力指數，會高估下一次減壓效益；相反，合法夜用水增加也可能掩蓋真實漏失下降，讓管理措施被誤判無效。","textEn":"Including leak removal from repairs in a pressure exponent overstates the benefit of a later pressure reduction. Conversely, increased legitimate night use can hide real leakage reduction and make the measure appear ineffective.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若把修復後漏點減少的效果算進壓力指數，會高估下一次減壓效益；相反，合法夜用水增加也可能掩蓋真實漏失下降，讓管理措施被誤判無效。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。"],"optionsEn":["Including leak removal from repairs in a pressure exponent overstates the benefit of a later pressure reduction.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若把修復後漏點減少的效果算進壓力指數，會高估下一次減壓效益；相反，合法夜用水增加也可能掩蓋真實漏失下降，讓管理措施被誤判無效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Including leak removal from repairs in a pressure exponent overstates the benefit of a later pressure reduction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b265-v15-13","title":"減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「減壓閥能量耗散」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Energy dissipation in reducing valves” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"減壓閥藉節流將一部分水力能轉成湍流、熱及振動，閥後壓力降低不代表能量被回收。壓差與通量共同決定耗散功率，而局部高速區可能涉及空化與噪音；設計需對照閥型、上下游絕對壓力及運轉範圍，不能只從平均壓差選擇設備。壓差乘流量是流體功率差，未乘任何發電效率；只有另設能量回收裝置並證實效率時，才能估可利用電力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「減壓閥能量耗散」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A pressure-reducing valve converts hydraulic energy into turbulence, heat and vibration through throttling; lower downstream pressure does not mean energy recovery. Pressure difference and flow determine dissipated power, while local high-speed zones may involve cavitation and noise. Equipment assessment needs valve type, absolute boundary pressures and operating range rather than average pressure drop alone. Pressure difference times flow is a fluid-power difference with no generation efficiency applied. Useful electric power requires a separate recovery device and substantiated efficiency. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Energy dissipation in reducing valves” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓差Δp=200 kPa、Q=0.020 m³/s，耗散水力功率P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW，不是發電量。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve drop Δp=200 kPa and Q=0.020 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「減壓閥能量耗散」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Energy dissipation in reducing valves”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-13-k1","title":"減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證","titleEn":"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification","text":"減壓閥藉節流將一部分水力能轉成湍流、熱及振動，閥後壓力降低不代表能量被回收。壓差與通量共同決定耗散功率，而局部高速區可能涉及空化與噪音；設計需對照閥型、上下游絕對壓力及運轉範圍，不能只從平均壓差選擇設備。","textEn":"A pressure-reducing valve converts hydraulic energy into turbulence, heat and vibration through throttling; lower downstream pressure does not mean energy recovery. Pressure difference and flow determine dissipated power, while local high-speed zones may involve cavitation and noise.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。","減壓閥藉節流將一部分水力能轉成湍流、熱及振動，閥後壓力降低不代表能量被回收。","控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。"],"optionsEn":["All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity.","A pressure-reducing valve converts hydraulic energy into turbulence, heat and vibration through throttling.","A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"減壓閥藉節流將一部分水力能轉成湍流、熱及振動，閥後壓力降低不代表能量被回收。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A pressure-reducing valve converts hydraulic energy into turbulence, heat and vibration through throttling; lower downstream pressure does not mean energy recovery. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b265-v15-14","title":"減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「減壓閥能量耗散」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Energy dissipation in reducing valves” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓差Δp=200 kPa、Q=0.020 m³/s，耗散水力功率P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW，不是發電量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve drop Δp=200 kPa and Q=0.020 m³/s. Dissipated hydraulic power P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW, not generated power. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測閥前後壓力與流量，核對壓力取樣點是否避開不適當的局部擾動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure upstream and downstream pressure with flow simultaneously, checking whether pressure taps are affected by unsuitable local disturbances.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓差Δp=200 kPa、Q=0.020 m³/s，耗散水力功率P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW，不是發電量。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve drop Δp=200 kPa and Q=0.020 m³/s. Dissipated hydraulic power P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW, not generated power.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。","平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓差Δp=200 kPa、Q=0.020 m³/s，耗散水力功率P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW，不是發電量。"],"optionsEn":["Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation.","Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve drop Δp=200 kPa and Q=0.020 m³/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓差Δp=200 kPa、Q=0.020 m³/s，耗散水力功率P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW，不是發電量。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve drop Δp=200 kPa and Q=0.020 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b265-v15-15","title":"減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「減壓閥能量耗散」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Energy dissipation in reducing valves” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測閥前後壓力與流量，核對壓力取樣點是否避開不適當的局部擾動。比較設備核定的壓差及流量範圍，並追蹤噪音、振動和內部損傷，避免只以能量帳判定設備適用性。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure upstream and downstream pressure with flow simultaneously, checking whether pressure taps are affected by unsuitable local disturbances. Compare the approved pressure-drop and flow range and track noise, vibration and internal damage instead of judging suitability from the energy ledger alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將同一壓差下兩個流量的耗散功率比較，另畫出有能量回收裝置時的效率鏈。明確區分功率與一段時間的能量，再列出設備適用性仍需的資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare dissipated power at two flows under one pressure drop and draw a separate efficiency chain for a recovery device. Distinguish power from time-integrated energy and list remaining equipment-suitability data.","failure":"注意干擾：把耗散功率寫成可回收發電功率會誇大效益，忽略局部低壓又可能漏掉空化損傷；閥後平均壓力正常並不能保證閥內最低壓力也正常。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reporting dissipated power as recoverable generation exaggerates benefits, while ignoring local low pressure misses possible cavitation damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測閥前後壓力與流量，核對壓力取樣點是否避開不適當的局部擾動。比較設備核定的壓差及流量範圍，並追蹤噪音、振動和內部損傷，避免只以能量帳判定設備適用性。","textEn":"Measure upstream and downstream pressure with flow simultaneously, checking whether pressure taps are affected by unsuitable local disturbances. Compare the approved pressure-drop and flow range and track noise, vibration and internal damage instead of judging suitability from the energy ledger alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將同一壓差下兩個流量的耗散功率比較，另畫出有能量回收裝置時的效率鏈。明確區分功率與一段時間的能量，再列出設備適用性仍需的資料。","textEn":"Compare dissipated power at two flows under one pressure drop and draw a separate efficiency chain for a recovery device. Distinguish power from time-integrated energy and list remaining equipment-suitability data.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification\"?","options":["同步量測閥前後壓力與流量，核對壓力取樣點是否避開不適當的局部擾動。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Measure upstream and downstream pressure with flow simultaneously, checking whether pressure taps are affected by unsuitable local disturbances.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步量測閥前後壓力與流量，核對壓力取樣點是否避開不適當的局部擾動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure upstream and downstream pressure with flow simultaneously, checking whether pressure taps are affected by unsuitable local disturbances. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b265-v15-16","title":"減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「減壓閥能量耗散」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Energy dissipation in reducing valves” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把耗散功率寫成可回收發電功率會誇大效益，忽略局部低壓又可能漏掉空化損傷；閥後平均壓力正常並不能保證閥內最低壓力也正常。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reporting dissipated power as recoverable generation exaggerates benefits, while ignoring local low pressure misses possible cavitation damage. Normal downstream mean pressure does not ensure an acceptable internal minimum pressure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：壓差乘流量是流體功率差，未乘任何發電效率；只有另設能量回收裝置並證實效率時，才能估可利用電力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Useful electric power requires a separate recovery device and substantiated efficiency.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把耗散功率寫成可回收發電功率會誇大效益，忽略局部低壓又可能漏掉空化損傷；閥後平均壓力正常並不能保證閥內最低壓力也正常。","textEn":"Reporting dissipated power as recoverable generation exaggerates benefits, while ignoring local low pressure misses possible cavitation damage. Normal downstream mean pressure does not ensure an acceptable internal minimum pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把耗散功率寫成可回收發電功率會誇大效益，忽略局部低壓又可能漏掉空化損傷；閥後平均壓力正常並不能保證閥內最低壓力也正常。","控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Reporting dissipated power as recoverable generation exaggerates benefits, while ignoring local low pressure misses possible cavitation damage.","A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把耗散功率寫成可回收發電功率會誇大效益，忽略局部低壓又可能漏掉空化損傷；閥後平均壓力正常並不能保證閥內最低壓力也正常。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reporting dissipated power as recoverable generation exaggerates benefits, while ignoring local low pressure misses possible cavitation damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b265-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證」與「遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification\" and \"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b265-v15-17","title":"閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「閥權度與穩定調節」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Valve authority and stable regulation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"控制閥的作用取決於自身壓降相對整個受控支路壓降的比例，閥位改變不一定帶來同樣比例的流量變化。閥過大時可能長期在很小開度工作，機械間隙與摩擦會放大調節困難；閥權度提供一種局部比較，但不能單獨描述導閥、控制器與管網的動態穩定性。此比值在同一工況下分開閥門與其餘支路損失，沒有給出通用合格門檻；實際控制增益還取決於閥特性與邊界。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「閥權度與穩定調節」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A control valve’s influence depends on its pressure drop relative to the controlled branch, so a position change does not necessarily produce a proportional flow change. An oversized valve may operate near closure where backlash and friction complicate regulation. Valve authority offers a local comparison but cannot by itself describe pilot, controller and network dynamic stability. The ratio separates valve loss from the rest of the branch at one condition and supplies no universal acceptance threshold. Actual control gain also depends on valve characteristic and boundaries. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Valve authority and stable regulation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓降hv=20 m、其餘受控支路損失hr=30 m，權度Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40，為指定工況比較。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve loss hv=20 m and remaining controlled-branch loss hr=30 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「閥權度與穩定調節」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Valve authority and stable regulation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-17-k1","title":"閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證","titleEn":"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification","text":"控制閥的作用取決於自身壓降相對整個受控支路壓降的比例，閥位改變不一定帶來同樣比例的流量變化。閥過大時可能長期在很小開度工作，機械間隙與摩擦會放大調節困難；閥權度提供一種局部比較，但不能單獨描述導閥、控制器與管網的動態穩定性。","textEn":"A control valve’s influence depends on its pressure drop relative to the controlled branch, so a position change does not necessarily produce a proportional flow change. An oversized valve may operate near closure where backlash and friction complicate regulation.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。","通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","控制閥的作用取決於自身壓降相對整個受控支路壓降的比例，閥位改變不一定帶來同樣比例的流量變化。"],"optionsEn":["A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow.","A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","A control valve’s influence depends on its pressure drop relative to the controlled branch, so a position change does not necessarily produce a proportional flow change."],"answer":2,"explanation":"控制閥的作用取決於自身壓降相對整個受控支路壓降的比例，閥位改變不一定帶來同樣比例的流量變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A control valve’s influence depends on its pressure drop relative to the controlled branch, so a position change does not necessarily produce a proportional flow change. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b265-v15-18","title":"閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「閥權度與穩定調節」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Valve authority and stable regulation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓降hv=20 m、其餘受控支路損失hr=30 m，權度Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40，為指定工況比較。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve loss hv=20 m and remaining controlled-branch loss hr=30 m. Authority Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40 for the specified operating condition. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：取得閥位、流量係數與實測壓差關係，檢查低流量及高流量時是否仍具可調範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Obtain valve-position, flow-coefficient and measured-drop relationships, checking controllable range at low and high flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓降hv=20 m、其餘受控支路損失hr=30 m，權度Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40，為指定工況比較。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve loss hv=20 m and remaining controlled-branch loss hr=30 m. Authority Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40 for the specified operating condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓降hv=20 m、其餘受控支路損失hr=30 m，權度Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40，為指定工況比較。","現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。","壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve loss hv=20 m and remaining controlled-branch loss hr=30 m.","Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario.","Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓降hv=20 m、其餘受控支路損失hr=30 m，權度Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40，為指定工況比較。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve loss hv=20 m and remaining controlled-branch loss hr=30 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b265-v15-19","title":"閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「閥權度與穩定調節」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Valve authority and stable regulation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"取得閥位、流量係數與實測壓差關係，檢查低流量及高流量時是否仍具可調範圍。將導閥、摩擦遲滯與控制器時間尺度納入離線模型，以實際穩態和小擾動資料交叉驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Obtain valve-position, flow-coefficient and measured-drop relationships, checking controllable range at low and high flow. Include pilot dynamics, frictional hysteresis and controller time scales in offline modeling, cross-checking against observed steady states and small disturbances. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在相同邊界下比較兩種假設閥特性，標出日常工況落在哪個開度區間。使用權度解釋局部敏感性，同時列出它無法判斷的動態與機械問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare two hypothetical valve characteristics under identical boundaries, marking their normal operating openings. Use authority to explain local sensitivity while listing dynamic and mechanical issues it cannot resolve.","failure":"注意干擾：只按最大流量選擇很大閥徑，可能讓日常操作落在難以控制的小開度；反覆小幅動作會增加磨耗與壓力波動，即使最大供量仍能達到。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sizing a valve only for maximum flow can place ordinary operation in a poorly controllable near-closed range. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"取得閥位、流量係數與實測壓差關係，檢查低流量及高流量時是否仍具可調範圍。將導閥、摩擦遲滯與控制器時間尺度納入離線模型，以實際穩態和小擾動資料交叉驗證。","textEn":"Obtain valve-position, flow-coefficient and measured-drop relationships, checking controllable range at low and high flow. Include pilot dynamics, frictional hysteresis and controller time scales in offline modeling, cross-checking against observed steady states and small disturbances.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在相同邊界下比較兩種假設閥特性，標出日常工況落在哪個開度區間。使用權度解釋局部敏感性，同時列出它無法判斷的動態與機械問題。","textEn":"Compare two hypothetical valve characteristics under identical boundaries, marking their normal operating openings. Use authority to explain local sensitivity while listing dynamic and mechanical issues it cannot resolve.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","取得閥位、流量係數與實測壓差關係，檢查低流量及高流量時是否仍具可調範圍。","管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Obtain valve-position, flow-coefficient and measured-drop relationships, checking controllable range at low and high flow.","A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"取得閥位、流量係數與實測壓差關係，檢查低流量及高流量時是否仍具可調範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Obtain valve-position, flow-coefficient and measured-drop relationships, checking controllable range at low and high flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b265-v15-20","title":"閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「閥權度與穩定調節」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Valve authority and stable regulation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只按最大流量選擇很大閥徑，可能讓日常操作落在難以控制的小開度；反覆小幅動作會增加磨耗與壓力波動，即使最大供量仍能達到。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sizing a valve only for maximum flow can place ordinary operation in a poorly controllable near-closed range. Repeated small movements increase wear and pressure fluctuation even when maximum delivery remains adequate. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此比值在同一工況下分開閥門與其餘支路損失，沒有給出通用合格門檻；實際控制增益還取決於閥特性與邊界。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Actual control gain also depends on valve characteristic and boundaries.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只按最大流量選擇很大閥徑，可能讓日常操作落在難以控制的小開度；反覆小幅動作會增加磨耗與壓力波動，即使最大供量仍能達到。","textEn":"Sizing a valve only for maximum flow can place ordinary operation in a poorly controllable near-closed range. Repeated small movements increase wear and pressure fluctuation even when maximum delivery remains adequate.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","只按最大流量選擇很大閥徑，可能讓日常操作落在難以控制的小開度；反覆小幅動作會增加磨耗與壓力波動，即使最大供量仍能達到。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","Sizing a valve only for maximum flow can place ordinary operation in a poorly controllable near-closed range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只按最大流量選擇很大閥徑，可能讓日常操作落在難以控制的小開度；反覆小幅動作會增加磨耗與壓力波動，即使最大供量仍能達到。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sizing a valve only for maximum flow can place ordinary operation in a poorly controllable near-closed range. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b265-v15-21","title":"遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Remote pressure and communication delay” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以遠端服務點回授可改善代表性，但通訊延遲使控制器看到的是過去狀態而非當前壓力。需求快速增加時，延遲期間的壓降可能已消耗原有裕度；資料時間戳、封包重送與感測器濾波都會增加有效滯後，不能只把無線傳輸的名目速度當整體延遲。線性變化率乘延遲只估未觀測的水頭改變，並非實際控制響應；需求突變與非線性管網仍需另外模擬。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Remote service-point feedback can improve representation, but communication delay means the controller sees a past state rather than current pressure. During rising demand, pressure can consume its available margin before the update arrives. Timestamps, retransmission and sensor filtering all add effective lag, so nominal wireless transmission speed does not equal total feedback delay. A linear rate times delay estimates unobserved head change, not actual closed-loop response. Demand steps and nonlinear network behavior still require separate modeling. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Remote pressure and communication delay” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭變化率dh/dt=−0.020 m/s、總延遲τ=180 s，未觀測變化Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head-change rate dh/dt=−0.020 m/s and total delay τ=180 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Remote pressure and communication delay”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-21-k1","title":"遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證","titleEn":"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification","text":"以遠端服務點回授可改善代表性，但通訊延遲使控制器看到的是過去狀態而非當前壓力。需求快速增加時，延遲期間的壓降可能已消耗原有裕度；資料時間戳、封包重送與感測器濾波都會增加有效滯後，不能只把無線傳輸的名目速度當整體延遲。","textEn":"Remote service-point feedback can improve representation, but communication delay means the controller sees a past state rather than current pressure. During rising demand, pressure can consume its available margin before the update arrives.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["以遠端服務點回授可改善代表性，但通訊延遲使控制器看到的是過去狀態而非當前壓力。","通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。"],"optionsEn":["Remote service-point feedback can improve representation, but communication delay means the controller sees a past state rather than current pressure.","A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以遠端服務點回授可改善代表性，但通訊延遲使控制器看到的是過去狀態而非當前壓力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Remote service-point feedback can improve representation, but communication delay means the controller sees a past state rather than current pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b265-v15-22","title":"遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Remote pressure and communication delay” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭變化率dh/dt=−0.020 m/s、總延遲τ=180 s，未觀測變化Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head-change rate dh/dt=−0.020 m/s and total delay τ=180 s. Unobserved change Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從感測器採樣到控制器使用資料的整條路徑量測延遲，保留來源時間與接收時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure delay from sensor sampling to actual controller use, retaining source and receipt timestamps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭變化率dh/dt=−0.020 m/s、總延遲τ=180 s，未觀測變化Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head-change rate dh/dt=−0.020 m/s and total delay τ=180 s. Unobserved change Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭變化率dh/dt=−0.020 m/s、總延遲τ=180 s，未觀測變化Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m。","減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head-change rate dh/dt=−0.020 m/s and total delay τ=180 s.","Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭變化率dh/dt=−0.020 m/s、總延遲τ=180 s，未觀測變化Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head-change rate dh/dt=−0.020 m/s and total delay τ=180 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b265-v15-23","title":"遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Remote pressure and communication delay” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從感測器採樣到控制器使用資料的整條路徑量測延遲，保留來源時間與接收時間。對缺值、重送及過期資料建立可辨識標記，在離線情境中檢查失去遠端訊號時的核定備援行為。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure delay from sensor sampling to actual controller use, retaining source and receipt timestamps. Flag missing, retransmitted and stale records explicitly and examine the approved fallback behavior during loss of remote signals in offline scenarios. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出採樣、傳送、重送與使用四個時間點，分開資料新鮮度與連線狀態。用假設壓力斜率估延遲影響，再說明核定控制設計應如何驗證過期資料處理。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw sampling, transmission, retransmission and use timestamps, separating data freshness from link status. Estimate delay effect with a hypothetical pressure slope and explain how approved control design should verify stale-data handling.","failure":"注意干擾：控制器若將重送的舊壓力當成新資料，可能反向修正已經恢復的壓力，造成反覆追逐與振盪；通訊恢復也不等於所有歷史封包都可立即參與控制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If a controller treats retransmitted old pressure as current, it can counteract a pressure condition that has already recovered and create repeated chasing or oscillation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從感測器採樣到控制器使用資料的整條路徑量測延遲，保留來源時間與接收時間。對缺值、重送及過期資料建立可辨識標記，在離線情境中檢查失去遠端訊號時的核定備援行為。","textEn":"Measure delay from sensor sampling to actual controller use, retaining source and receipt timestamps. Flag missing, retransmitted and stale records explicitly and examine the approved fallback behavior during loss of remote signals in offline scenarios.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出採樣、傳送、重送與使用四個時間點，分開資料新鮮度與連線狀態。用假設壓力斜率估延遲影響，再說明核定控制設計應如何驗證過期資料處理。","textEn":"Draw sampling, transmission, retransmission and use timestamps, separating data freshness from link status. Estimate delay effect with a hypothetical pressure slope and explain how approved control design should verify stale-data handling.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。","從感測器採樣到控制器使用資料的整條路徑量測延遲，保留來源時間與接收時間。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.","Measure delay from sensor sampling to actual controller use, retaining source and receipt timestamps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"從感測器採樣到控制器使用資料的整條路徑量測延遲，保留來源時間與接收時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure delay from sensor sampling to actual controller use, retaining source and receipt timestamps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b265-v15-24","title":"遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Remote pressure and communication delay” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"控制器若將重送的舊壓力當成新資料，可能反向修正已經恢復的壓力，造成反覆追逐與振盪；通訊恢復也不等於所有歷史封包都可立即參與控制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If a controller treats retransmitted old pressure as current, it can counteract a pressure condition that has already recovered and create repeated chasing or oscillation. Restored communication does not make every historical packet suitable for immediate control. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：線性變化率乘延遲只估未觀測的水頭改變，並非實際控制響應；需求突變與非線性管網仍需另外模擬。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demand steps and nonlinear network behavior still require separate modeling.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"控制器若將重送的舊壓力當成新資料，可能反向修正已經恢復的壓力，造成反覆追逐與振盪；通訊恢復也不等於所有歷史封包都可立即參與控制。","textEn":"If a controller treats retransmitted old pressure as current, it can counteract a pressure condition that has already recovered and create repeated chasing or oscillation. Restored communication does not make every historical packet suitable for immediate control.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["控制器若將重送的舊壓力當成新資料，可能反向修正已經恢復的壓力，造成反覆追逐與振盪；通訊恢復也不等於所有歷史封包都可立即參與控制。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。"],"optionsEn":["If a controller treats retransmitted old pressure as current, it can counteract a pressure condition that has already recovered and create repeated chasing or oscillation.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"控制器若將重送的舊壓力當成新資料，可能反向修正已經恢復的壓力，造成反覆追逐與振盪；通訊恢復也不等於所有歷史封包都可立即參與控制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If a controller treats retransmitted old pressure as current, it can counteract a pressure condition that has already recovered and create repeated chasing or oscillation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b265-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證」與「備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification\" and \"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b265-v15-25","title":"回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「回授增益與控制方向」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Feedback gain and control direction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓力回授必須先確認誤差符號與閥門作用方向，否則負回授可能被接成正回授。比例增益把壓力誤差轉成控制量，但實際壓力還受閥特性、管網儲能及延遲影響；提高增益未必改善速度，積分飽和與機械死區可能讓系統反而反覆超越目標。本式只是指定符號的控制量算術，不是可直接投入現場的增益；正百分點方向必須由設備作用定義，不假設等於開閥。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「回授增益與控制方向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pressure feedback first needs consistent error sign and valve action, or intended negative feedback becomes positive feedback. Proportional gain converts pressure error into a command, while actual pressure also depends on valve characteristics, network storage and delay. Higher gain need not improve response; integral saturation and mechanical deadband can instead create repeated overshoot. This is command arithmetic under a declared sign convention, not a field-ready gain. The positive percentage-point direction must be defined by equipment action and is not presumed to mean opening. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Feedback gain and control direction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設誤差e=目標−量測=5 m、比較增益Kp=0.40百分點/m，比例命令Δu=Kp e=2.0百分點；未計動態。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume error e=target−measured=5 m and comparison gain Kp=0.40 percentage points/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「回授增益與控制方向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Feedback gain and control direction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-25-k1","title":"回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證","titleEn":"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification","text":"壓力回授必須先確認誤差符號與閥門作用方向，否則負回授可能被接成正回授。比例增益把壓力誤差轉成控制量，但實際壓力還受閥特性、管網儲能及延遲影響；提高增益未必改善速度，積分飽和與機械死區可能讓系統反而反覆超越目標。","textEn":"Pressure feedback first needs consistent error sign and valve action, or intended negative feedback becomes positive feedback. Proportional gain converts pressure error into a command, while actual pressure also depends on valve characteristics, network storage and delay.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。","壓力回授必須先確認誤差符號與閥門作用方向，否則負回授可能被接成正回授。","現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。"],"optionsEn":["Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation.","Pressure feedback first needs consistent error sign and valve action, or intended negative feedback becomes positive feedback.","Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario."],"answer":1,"explanation":"壓力回授必須先確認誤差符號與閥門作用方向，否則負回授可能被接成正回授。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pressure feedback first needs consistent error sign and valve action, or intended negative feedback becomes positive feedback. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b265-v15-26","title":"回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「回授增益與控制方向」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Feedback gain and control direction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設誤差e=目標−量測=5 m、比較增益Kp=0.40百分點/m，比例命令Δu=Kp e=2.0百分點；未計動態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume error e=target−measured=5 m and comparison gain Kp=0.40 percentage points/m. Proportional command Δu=Kp e=2.0 percentage points, excluding dynamics. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在離線模型確認誤差與設備方向，再檢查命令限制、死區及回授延遲。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm error and device direction in an offline model, then inspect command limits, deadband and feedback delay.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設誤差e=目標−量測=5 m、比較增益Kp=0.40百分點/m，比例命令Δu=Kp e=2.0百分點；未計動態。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume error e=target−measured=5 m and comparison gain Kp=0.40 percentage points/m. Proportional command Δu=Kp e=2.0 percentage points, excluding dynamics.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。","管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設誤差e=目標−量測=5 m、比較增益Kp=0.40百分點/m，比例命令Δu=Kp e=2.0百分點；未計動態。"],"optionsEn":["Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality.","A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume error e=target−measured=5 m and comparison gain Kp=0.40 percentage points/m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設誤差e=目標−量測=5 m、比較增益Kp=0.40百分點/m，比例命令Δu=Kp e=2.0百分點；未計動態。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume error e=target−measured=5 m and comparison gain Kp=0.40 percentage points/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b265-v15-27","title":"回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「回授增益與控制方向」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Feedback gain and control direction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在離線模型確認誤差與設備方向，再檢查命令限制、死區及回授延遲。以核准測試資料比較目標、量測、閥位與控制命令，確認任何飽和或失訊時均使用已設計的行為。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm error and device direction in an offline model, then inspect command limits, deadband and feedback delay. Compare target, measurement, position and command using approved test records, verifying designed behavior during saturation or signal loss. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用兩種相反的設備方向畫出回授符號圖，判斷哪一種形成負回授。把簡單命令計算與完整動態驗證分開，列出延遲及飽和需要的額外情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw feedback-sign diagrams for two opposite device actions and identify negative feedback. Separate command arithmetic from dynamic validation, listing additional delay and saturation scenarios needed.","failure":"注意干擾：符號設定錯誤會讓低壓時的動作進一步降低壓力，形成正回授；增益過高還可能使閥位頻繁反轉，增加磨耗並把控制波動傳到用戶端。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An incorrect sign can make the response to low pressure reduce pressure further, creating positive feedback. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在離線模型確認誤差與設備方向，再檢查命令限制、死區及回授延遲。以核准測試資料比較目標、量測、閥位與控制命令，確認任何飽和或失訊時均使用已設計的行為。","textEn":"Confirm error and device direction in an offline model, then inspect command limits, deadband and feedback delay. Compare target, measurement, position and command using approved test records, verifying designed behavior during saturation or signal loss.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用兩種相反的設備方向畫出回授符號圖，判斷哪一種形成負回授。把簡單命令計算與完整動態驗證分開，列出延遲及飽和需要的額外情境。","textEn":"Draw feedback-sign diagrams for two opposite device actions and identify negative feedback. Separate command arithmetic from dynamic validation, listing additional delay and saturation scenarios needed.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification\"?","options":["在離線模型確認誤差與設備方向，再檢查命令限制、死區及回授延遲。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。"],"optionsEn":["Confirm error and device direction in an offline model, then inspect command limits, deadband and feedback delay.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在離線模型確認誤差與設備方向，再檢查命令限制、死區及回授延遲。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm error and device direction in an offline model, then inspect command limits, deadband and feedback delay. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b265-v15-28","title":"回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「回授增益與控制方向」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Feedback gain and control direction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"符號設定錯誤會讓低壓時的動作進一步降低壓力，形成正回授；增益過高還可能使閥位頻繁反轉，增加磨耗並把控制波動傳到用戶端。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An incorrect sign can make the response to low pressure reduce pressure further, creating positive feedback. Excessive gain can also reverse valve motion repeatedly, increasing wear and transmitting control oscillations to customers. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本式只是指定符號的控制量算術，不是可直接投入現場的增益；正百分點方向必須由設備作用定義，不假設等於開閥。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The positive percentage-point direction must be defined by equipment action and is not presumed to mean opening.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"符號設定錯誤會讓低壓時的動作進一步降低壓力，形成正回授；增益過高還可能使閥位頻繁反轉，增加磨耗並把控制波動傳到用戶端。","textEn":"An incorrect sign can make the response to low pressure reduce pressure further, creating positive feedback. Excessive gain can also reverse valve motion repeatedly, increasing wear and transmitting control oscillations to customers.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","符號設定錯誤會讓低壓時的動作進一步降低壓力，形成正回授；增益過高還可能使閥位頻繁反轉，增加磨耗並把控制波動傳到用戶端。","現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","An incorrect sign can make the response to low pressure reduce pressure further, creating positive feedback.","Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario."],"answer":1,"explanation":"符號設定錯誤會讓低壓時的動作進一步降低壓力，形成正回授；增益過高還可能使閥位頻繁反轉，增加磨耗並把控制波動傳到用戶端。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An incorrect sign can make the response to low pressure reduce pressure further, creating positive feedback. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b265-v15-29","title":"備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「備援供水與非常態邊界」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓力管理設備檢修或失效時，替代供水路徑的水頭損失可能不同於正常路徑。備援管路存在不代表備援服務能力足夠，較小管徑、較長距離或不同水源高程都會降低遠端壓力；評估需按實際可用的水源與閥位重建網路，而不是把名目容量直接相加。此例只檢查一個指定備援工況的水頭餘量，不包含水源可用性、消防需求與瞬變；負餘量表示假設條件未滿足比較需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「備援供水與非常態邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"During maintenance or failure of pressure-management equipment, an alternative supply path can have different head losses from the normal route. A bypass does not guarantee adequate backup service: smaller diameter, longer length or another source elevation can reduce remote pressure. Assessment must reconstruct actual available sources and valve states instead of simply adding nominal capacities. The example checks head margin for one backup condition, excluding source availability, fire demand and transients. A negative margin means the assumed case does not meet the comparison requirement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設備援水頭45 m、節點高程20 m、損失18 m，h=7 m；比較需求15 m，餘量h−hreq=−8 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume backup head 45 m, node elevation 20 m and loss 18 m, giving h=7 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「備援供水與非常態邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-29-k1","title":"備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證","titleEn":"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification","text":"壓力管理設備檢修或失效時，替代供水路徑的水頭損失可能不同於正常路徑。備援管路存在不代表備援服務能力足夠，較小管徑、較長距離或不同水源高程都會降低遠端壓力；評估需按實際可用的水源與閥位重建網路，而不是把名目容量直接相加。","textEn":"During maintenance or failure of pressure-management equipment, an alternative supply path can have different head losses from the normal route. A bypass does not guarantee adequate backup service: smaller diameter, longer length or another source elevation can reduce remote pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。","平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。","壓力管理設備檢修或失效時，替代供水路徑的水頭損失可能不同於正常路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario.","Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.","During maintenance or failure of pressure-management equipment, an alternative supply path can have different head losses from the normal route."],"answer":2,"explanation":"壓力管理設備檢修或失效時，替代供水路徑的水頭損失可能不同於正常路徑。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"During maintenance or failure of pressure-management equipment, an alternative supply path can have different head losses from the normal route. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b265-v15-30","title":"備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「備援供水與非常態邊界」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設備援水頭45 m、節點高程20 m、損失18 m，h=7 m；比較需求15 m，餘量h−hreq=−8 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume backup head 45 m, node elevation 20 m and loss 18 m, giving h=7 m. Against comparison requirement 15 m, margin h−hreq=−8 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對備援水源、旁通閥及相鄰分區可承受的供量，對正常和失效狀態各保存一份拓樸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify backup sources, bypass valves and neighboring-district supply availability, retaining separate normal and failed-state topologies.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設備援水頭45 m、節點高程20 m、損失18 m，h=7 m；比較需求15 m，餘量h−hreq=−8 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume backup head 45 m, node elevation 20 m and loss 18 m, giving h=7 m. Against comparison requirement 15 m, margin h−hreq=−8 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設備援水頭45 m、節點高程20 m、損失18 m，h=7 m；比較需求15 m，餘量h−hreq=−8 m。","減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。","漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume backup head 45 m, node elevation 20 m and loss 18 m, giving h=7 m.","Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer.","The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設備援水頭45 m、節點高程20 m、損失18 m，h=7 m；比較需求15 m，餘量h−hreq=−8 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume backup head 45 m, node elevation 20 m and loss 18 m, giving h=7 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b265-v15-31","title":"備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「備援供水與非常態邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對備援水源、旁通閥及相鄰分區可承受的供量，對正常和失效狀態各保存一份拓樸。以代表需求組合重算遠端壓力，檢查備援切換是否把缺壓轉移到其他服務區。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify backup sources, bypass valves and neighboring-district supply availability, retaining separate normal and failed-state topologies. Recompute remote pressure for representative demand combinations and check whether backup switching transfers a pressure deficit to another service area. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對同一需求分別畫出正常與備援水頭線，標出哪段損失增加。列出可能共同失效的水源、電力及通訊依賴，避免把名義上兩條路徑當成完全獨立備援。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw normal and backup hydraulic grades for one demand, identifying increased losses. List shared source, power and communications dependencies so two nominal paths are not mistaken for fully independent backup.","failure":"注意干擾：只確認旁通閥能開啟而未檢查路徑損失，可能在真正需要備援時才發現供壓不足；借用相鄰區水頭又可能使另一區同時失去服務裕度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking only that a bypass valve can open can leave inadequate pressure undiscovered until backup is needed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對備援水源、旁通閥及相鄰分區可承受的供量，對正常和失效狀態各保存一份拓樸。以代表需求組合重算遠端壓力，檢查備援切換是否把缺壓轉移到其他服務區。","textEn":"Verify backup sources, bypass valves and neighboring-district supply availability, retaining separate normal and failed-state topologies. Recompute remote pressure for representative demand combinations and check whether backup switching transfers a pressure deficit to another service area.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對同一需求分別畫出正常與備援水頭線，標出哪段損失增加。列出可能共同失效的水源、電力及通訊依賴，避免把名義上兩條路徑當成完全獨立備援。","textEn":"Draw normal and backup hydraulic grades for one demand, identifying increased losses. List shared source, power and communications dependencies so two nominal paths are not mistaken for fully independent backup.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對備援水源、旁通閥及相鄰分區可承受的供量，對正常和失效狀態各保存一份拓樸。","控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Verify backup sources, bypass valves and neighboring-district supply availability, retaining separate normal and failed-state topologies.","A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對備援水源、旁通閥及相鄰分區可承受的供量，對正常和失效狀態各保存一份拓樸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify backup sources, bypass valves and neighboring-district supply availability, retaining separate normal and failed-state topologies. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b265-v15-32","title":"備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「備援供水與非常態邊界」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只確認旁通閥能開啟而未檢查路徑損失，可能在真正需要備援時才發現供壓不足；借用相鄰區水頭又可能使另一區同時失去服務裕度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking only that a bypass valve can open can leave inadequate pressure undiscovered until backup is needed. Drawing on a neighboring district’s head may also remove its service margin at the same time. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此例只檢查一個指定備援工況的水頭餘量，不包含水源可用性、消防需求與瞬變；負餘量表示假設條件未滿足比較需求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A negative margin means the assumed case does not meet the comparison requirement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只確認旁通閥能開啟而未檢查路徑損失，可能在真正需要備援時才發現供壓不足；借用相鄰區水頭又可能使另一區同時失去服務裕度。","textEn":"Checking only that a bypass valve can open can leave inadequate pressure undiscovered until backup is needed. Drawing on a neighboring district’s head may also remove its service margin at the same time.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。","只確認旁通閥能開啟而未檢查路徑損失，可能在真正需要備援時才發現供壓不足；借用相鄰區水頭又可能使另一區同時失去服務裕度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.","Checking only that a bypass valve can open can leave inadequate pressure undiscovered until backup is needed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只確認旁通閥能開啟而未檢查路徑損失，可能在真正需要備援時才發現供壓不足；借用相鄰區水頭又可能使另一區同時失去服務裕度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking only that a bypass valve can open can leave inadequate pressure undiscovered until backup is needed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b265-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證」與「低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification\" and \"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b265-v15-33","title":"調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「調壓動作與快速瞬變」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"降低長期平均壓力不代表每一次調節都降低瞬間峰值，過快閥動作會改變流速並激發壓力波。控制器時間尺度與管線波傳時間可能相差很大，延時管網模型無法解析快速水錘；因此壓力管理方案需把服務水頭、控制動態及瞬變包絡分開而又一致地驗證。焦可夫斯基算例只估單一快速波前的壓力增量，不是閥動作建議，也不包含反射、低壓空穴及其他設備邊界。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「調壓動作與快速瞬變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lower long-term mean pressure does not guarantee lower instantaneous peaks during every adjustment. Rapid valve motion changes velocity and launches pressure waves. Controller and wave-travel time scales can differ greatly, and an extended-period network model cannot resolve fast water hammer. Service head, control dynamics and transient envelopes therefore need separate but consistent verification. The Joukowsky example estimates one rapid wavefront’s increment only. It is not a valve-action recommendation and excludes reflections, low-pressure cavities and other equipment boundaries. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=800 m/s、快速速度變化幅度Δv=0.20 m/s，Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa，須另加初始壓力。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=800 m/s and rapid velocity-change magnitude Δv=0.20 m/s. Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa, separate from initial pressure.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「調壓動作與快速瞬變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-33-k1","title":"調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification","text":"降低長期平均壓力不代表每一次調節都降低瞬間峰值，過快閥動作會改變流速並激發壓力波。控制器時間尺度與管線波傳時間可能相差很大，延時管網模型無法解析快速水錘；因此壓力管理方案需把服務水頭、控制動態及瞬變包絡分開而又一致地驗證。","textEn":"Lower long-term mean pressure does not guarantee lower instantaneous peaks during every adjustment. Rapid valve motion changes velocity and launches pressure waves.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["降低長期平均壓力不代表每一次調節都降低瞬間峰值，過快閥動作會改變流速並激發壓力波。","平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。","壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。"],"optionsEn":["Lower long-term mean pressure does not guarantee lower instantaneous peaks during every adjustment.","Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.","Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"降低長期平均壓力不代表每一次調節都降低瞬間峰值，過快閥動作會改變流速並激發壓力波。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lower long-term mean pressure does not guarantee lower instantaneous peaks during every adjustment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b265-v15-34","title":"調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「調壓動作與快速瞬變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=800 m/s、快速速度變化幅度Δv=0.20 m/s，Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa，須另加初始壓力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=800 m/s and rapid velocity-change magnitude Δv=0.20 m/s. Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa, separate from initial pressure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將閥位時間歷程與高速壓力紀錄同步，確認一般遙測是否足以看見短時尖峰。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize valve-position history with high-rate pressure records and check whether ordinary telemetry can resolve short peaks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=800 m/s、快速速度變化幅度Δv=0.20 m/s，Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa，須另加初始壓力。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=800 m/s and rapid velocity-change magnitude Δv=0.20 m/s. Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa, separate from initial pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=800 m/s、快速速度變化幅度Δv=0.20 m/s，Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa，須另加初始壓力。","減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。"],"optionsEn":["A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=800 m/s and rapid velocity-change magnitude Δv=0.20 m/s. Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa, separate from initial pressure.","All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=800 m/s、快速速度變化幅度Δv=0.20 m/s，Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa，須另加初始壓力。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=800 m/s and rapid velocity-change magnitude Δv=0.20 m/s. Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa, separate from initial pressure. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b265-v15-35","title":"調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「調壓動作與快速瞬變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將閥位時間歷程與高速壓力紀錄同步，確認一般遙測是否足以看見短時尖峰。使用相容的瞬變模型檢查正常調節、停電及失訊情境，再與延時模型的初始水頭及需求保持一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize valve-position history with high-rate pressure records and check whether ordinary telemetry can resolve short peaks. Use a compatible transient model for regulation, power loss and signal loss, keeping initial heads and demands consistent with the extended-period model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將一段含短時尖峰的假設壓力歷程做低頻平均，觀察哪些資訊消失。列出應用延時與瞬變模型的不同問題，並指出兩者需要共同保留的邊界資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Average a hypothetical pressure history containing a short peak and identify the information lost. List questions for extended-period and transient models and the boundary data that both must share.","failure":"注意干擾：只看每十五分鐘平均壓力可能完全漏掉秒級壓峰，讓減壓措施被誤判為同時解決所有水錘；快速回授反覆動作也可能增加管殼循環應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fifteen-minute mean pressure can completely miss second-scale peaks and falsely suggest that pressure reduction solved every transient. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將閥位時間歷程與高速壓力紀錄同步，確認一般遙測是否足以看見短時尖峰。使用相容的瞬變模型檢查正常調節、停電及失訊情境，再與延時模型的初始水頭及需求保持一致。","textEn":"Synchronize valve-position history with high-rate pressure records and check whether ordinary telemetry can resolve short peaks. Use a compatible transient model for regulation, power loss and signal loss, keeping initial heads and demands consistent with the extended-period model.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將一段含短時尖峰的假設壓力歷程做低頻平均，觀察哪些資訊消失。列出應用延時與瞬變模型的不同問題，並指出兩者需要共同保留的邊界資料。","textEn":"Average a hypothetical pressure history containing a short peak and identify the information lost. List questions for extended-period and transient models and the boundary data that both must share.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","將閥位時間歷程與高速壓力紀錄同步，確認一般遙測是否足以看見短時尖峰。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","Synchronize valve-position history with high-rate pressure records and check whether ordinary telemetry can resolve short peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將閥位時間歷程與高速壓力紀錄同步，確認一般遙測是否足以看見短時尖峰。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize valve-position history with high-rate pressure records and check whether ordinary telemetry can resolve short peaks. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b265-v15-36","title":"調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「調壓動作與快速瞬變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看每十五分鐘平均壓力可能完全漏掉秒級壓峰，讓減壓措施被誤判為同時解決所有水錘；快速回授反覆動作也可能增加管殼循環應力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fifteen-minute mean pressure can completely miss second-scale peaks and falsely suggest that pressure reduction solved every transient. Repeated rapid feedback actions can also increase cyclic shell stress. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：焦可夫斯基算例只估單一快速波前的壓力增量，不是閥動作建議，也不包含反射、低壓空穴及其他設備邊界。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is not a valve-action recommendation and excludes reflections, low-pressure cavities and other equipment boundaries.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看每十五分鐘平均壓力可能完全漏掉秒級壓峰，讓減壓措施被誤判為同時解決所有水錘；快速回授反覆動作也可能增加管殼循環應力。","textEn":"Fifteen-minute mean pressure can completely miss second-scale peaks and falsely suggest that pressure reduction solved every transient. Repeated rapid feedback actions can also increase cyclic shell stress.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只看每十五分鐘平均壓力可能完全漏掉秒級壓峰，讓減壓措施被誤判為同時解決所有水錘；快速回授反覆動作也可能增加管殼循環應力。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。"],"optionsEn":["Fifteen-minute mean pressure can completely miss second-scale peaks and falsely suggest that pressure reduction solved every transient.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只看每十五分鐘平均壓力可能完全漏掉秒級壓峰，讓減壓措施被誤判為同時解決所有水錘；快速回授反覆動作也可能增加管殼循環應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fifteen-minute mean pressure can completely miss second-scale peaks and falsely suggest that pressure reduction solved every transient. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b265-v15-37","title":"低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「低流量水齡與水質介面」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓力管理改變漏流與部分壓力相依需求後，某些支線的更新水量可能下降，水齡和消毒劑衰減便需要重新評估。幾何容積除以通量只給理想平均停留尺度，實際管網有混合、短路及死端分布；不能以較少水量損失直接推定所有水質指標都會改善。本例假設固定容積與穩定通量，只計平均尺度；它不是所有水粒子的年齡，也沒有提供任何水質合格判準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「低流量水齡與水質介面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After pressure management changes leakage and some pressure-dependent demand, renewal flow in certain branches can decrease, requiring reassessment of water age and disinfectant decay. Volume divided by flow gives an ideal mean residence scale, while actual networks contain mixing, short circuits and dead ends. Reduced physical loss therefore does not directly establish improvement in every water-quality indicator. The example assumes fixed volume and steady throughput to calculate a mean scale only. It is not the age of every water parcel and supplies no water-quality acceptance criterion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設支路有效水量V=500 m³、更新通量Q=10 m³/h，平均停留尺度τ=V/Q=50 h；若Q降至8 m³/h，τ=62.5 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective branch volume V=500 m³ and renewal flow Q=10 m³/h.","failure":"常見誤解：「壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「低流量水齡與水質介面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-37-k1","title":"低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證","titleEn":"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification","text":"壓力管理改變漏流與部分壓力相依需求後，某些支線的更新水量可能下降，水齡和消毒劑衰減便需要重新評估。幾何容積除以通量只給理想平均停留尺度，實際管網有混合、短路及死端分布；不能以較少水量損失直接推定所有水質指標都會改善。","textEn":"After pressure management changes leakage and some pressure-dependent demand, renewal flow in certain branches can decrease, requiring reassessment of water age and disinfectant decay. Volume divided by flow gives an ideal mean residence scale, while actual networks contain mixing, short circuits and dead ends.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。","壓力管理改變漏流與部分壓力相依需求後，某些支線的更新水量可能下降，水齡和消毒劑衰減便需要重新評估。","減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality.","After pressure management changes leakage and some pressure-dependent demand, renewal flow in certain branches can decrease, requiring reassessment of water age and disinfectant decay.","Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"壓力管理改變漏流與部分壓力相依需求後，某些支線的更新水量可能下降，水齡和消毒劑衰減便需要重新評估。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After pressure management changes leakage and some pressure-dependent demand, renewal flow in certain branches can decrease, requiring reassessment of water age and disinfectant decay. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b265-v15-38","title":"低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「低流量水齡與水質介面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設支路有效水量V=500 m³、更新通量Q=10 m³/h，平均停留尺度τ=V/Q=50 h；若Q降至8 m³/h，τ=62.5 h。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective branch volume V=500 m³ and renewal flow Q=10 m³/h. Mean residence scale τ=V/Q=50 h; at Q=8 m³/h, τ=62.5 h. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將壓力管理前後的流量、溫度及水質採樣位置對齊，使用適當管網水質模型檢查死端與水池混合。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align pre- and post-management flow, temperature and water-quality sampling locations, using an appropriate network-quality model to examine dead ends and tank mixing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設支路有效水量V=500 m³、更新通量Q=10 m³/h，平均停留尺度τ=V/Q=50 h；若Q降至8 m³/h，τ=62.5 h。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective branch volume V=500 m³ and renewal flow Q=10 m³/h. Mean residence scale τ=V/Q=50 h; at Q=8 m³/h, τ=62.5 h.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。","控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設支路有效水量V=500 m³、更新通量Q=10 m³/h，平均停留尺度τ=V/Q=50 h。"],"optionsEn":["The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.","A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective branch volume V=500 m³ and renewal flow Q=10 m³/h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設支路有效水量V=500 m³、更新通量Q=10 m³/h，平均停留尺度τ=V/Q=50 h；若Q降至8 m³/h，τ=62.5 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective branch volume V=500 m³ and renewal flow Q=10 m³/h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b265-v15-39","title":"低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「低流量水齡與水質介面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將壓力管理前後的流量、溫度及水質採樣位置對齊，使用適當管網水質模型檢查死端與水池混合。保留代表性時段及實測殘留資料，避免只用平均停留時間代替水質驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align pre- and post-management flow, temperature and water-quality sampling locations, using an appropriate network-quality model to examine dead ends and tank mixing. Retain representative periods and measured residuals rather than substituting mean residence time for water-quality verification. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以相同支路容積比較兩個更新通量的停留尺度，再說明死端與混合會如何改變年齡分布。把節水、供壓與水質列成三個需要共同驗證的成果。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare residence scales at two renewal flows for one branch volume, then explain how dead ends and mixing change the age distribution. Treat water savings, service pressure and quality as three outcomes requiring joint verification.","failure":"注意干擾：漏流減少後若忽略低更新支線，可能讓水齡增加而未被平均區壓監測發現；把理想停留尺度當成每個用戶的實際水齡，又會錯估局部水質風險。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring low-renewal branches after leakage reduction can allow water age to rise without appearing in average-pressure monitoring. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將壓力管理前後的流量、溫度及水質採樣位置對齊，使用適當管網水質模型檢查死端與水池混合。保留代表性時段及實測殘留資料，避免只用平均停留時間代替水質驗證。","textEn":"Align pre- and post-management flow, temperature and water-quality sampling locations, using an appropriate network-quality model to examine dead ends and tank mixing. Retain representative periods and measured residuals rather than substituting mean residence time for water-quality verification.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以相同支路容積比較兩個更新通量的停留尺度，再說明死端與混合會如何改變年齡分布。把節水、供壓與水質列成三個需要共同驗證的成果。","textEn":"Compare residence scales at two renewal flows for one branch volume, then explain how dead ends and mixing change the age distribution. Treat water savings, service pressure and quality as three outcomes requiring joint verification.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將壓力管理前後的流量、溫度及水質採樣位置對齊，使用適當管網水質模型檢查死端與水池混合。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。"],"optionsEn":["Align pre- and post-management flow, temperature and water-quality sampling locations, using an appropriate network-quality model to examine dead ends and tank mixing.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將壓力管理前後的流量、溫度及水質採樣位置對齊，使用適當管網水質模型檢查死端與水池混合。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align pre- and post-management flow, temperature and water-quality sampling locations, using an appropriate network-quality model to examine dead ends and tank mixing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b265-v15-40","title":"低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「低流量水齡與水質介面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏流減少後若忽略低更新支線，可能讓水齡增加而未被平均區壓監測發現；把理想停留尺度當成每個用戶的實際水齡，又會錯估局部水質風險。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring low-renewal branches after leakage reduction can allow water age to rise without appearing in average-pressure monitoring. Treating ideal residence scale as every customer’s actual water age also misrepresents localized quality concerns. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例假設固定容積與穩定通量，只計平均尺度；它不是所有水粒子的年齡，也沒有提供任何水質合格判準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is not the age of every water parcel and supplies no water-quality acceptance criterion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏流減少後若忽略低更新支線，可能讓水齡增加而未被平均區壓監測發現；把理想停留尺度當成每個用戶的實際水齡，又會錯估局部水質風險。","textEn":"Ignoring low-renewal branches after leakage reduction can allow water age to rise without appearing in average-pressure monitoring. Treating ideal residence scale as every customer’s actual water age also misrepresents localized quality concerns.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","漏流減少後若忽略低更新支線，可能讓水齡增加而未被平均區壓監測發現；把理想停留尺度當成每個用戶的實際水齡，又會錯估局部水質風險。","減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Ignoring low-renewal branches after leakage reduction can allow water age to rise without appearing in average-pressure monitoring.","Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"漏流減少後若忽略低更新支線，可能讓水齡增加而未被平均區壓監測發現；把理想停留尺度當成每個用戶的實際水齡，又會錯估局部水質風險。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring low-renewal branches after leakage reduction can allow water age to rise without appearing in average-pressure monitoring. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
